  "ConfigurationGuide": "Tracked in git and MUST NOT contain secrets: every secret-shaped value here is an empty string. This file is the schema of record — each section maps to an options class with an IValidateOptions validator and .ValidateOnStart(), so an incomplete or invalid configuration fails at STARTUP rather than on the first request. That is intentional: as shipped, this file alone will not boot the app. Supply the blanks with `dotnet user-secrets` locally or environment variables when deployed (double-underscore form, e.g. ConnectionStrings__Default, Jwt__Key). See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.",
